(708471, 73346, 18485, '<td valign="top">thanks all.  for anyone interested, this is a photo of a building in NYC.  i was in a taxi, late to meet a friend, and saw this fly by...glass facade with shiny protrusions.  i told the cabbie to stop (10 blocks from my destination) jumped out and started photographing the facade from as many angles as i could.  i chose this shot because it had the most "abstract" feel.  this was a fun exercise: it''s harder to find abstractions than i thought it would be.</td>', 'thanks all.  for anyone interested, this is a photo of a building in NYC.  i was in a taxi, late to meet a friend, and saw this fly by...glass facade with shiny protrusions.  i told the cabbie to stop (10 blocks from my destination) jumped out and started photographing the facade from as many angles as i could.  i chose this shot because it had the most "abstract" feel.  this was a fun exercise: it''s harder to find abstractions than i thought it would be.', '2004-05-10 08:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(708478, 72618, 20204, '<td valign="top">Well, this was an experiment gone bad judging by the 17th percentile it ranked.  It wasn''t at all dangerous to get the shot - the banks on either side are steep and I used a telephoto to make it look like I was actually up in the beams.  I had thought that by applying a gaussian blur it would make it more abstract than razor sharp lines.  I was wrong!  The original is a razor sharp image taken on a tripod, and I should have stuck with it.  I learned a lot in this challenge, so I''ll take the score and do better next time.</td>', 'Well, this was an experiment gone bad judging by the 17th percentile it ranked.  It wasn''t at all dangerous to get the shot - the banks on either side are steep and I used a telephoto to make it look like I was actually up in the beams.  I had thought that by applying a gaussian blur it would make it more abstract than razor sharp lines.  I was wrong!  The original is a razor sharp image taken on a tripod, and I should have stuck with it.  I learned a lot in this challenge, so I''ll take the score and do better next time.', '2004-05-10 09:05:35.000000', NULL, 0),
