(709224, 73268, 19780, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition: Very intresting. You have strong diagonal lines with excellent forced perspective. I question the crop of the photo - I think I''d like to see the louvers framed to start more to the left for a pleasing line that keeps the eye in frame. <br/> <br/>Background: great muted color and soft focus on the grid. <br/> <br/>Camera Work: (Focus/DOF/Exposure) Great DOF and focus on the foreground elements. The edges are nice and crisp and add to the color difference along the edge. <br/> <br/>Post Processing: n/a<br/> <br/>The Challenge: Wonderful abstract, great muted colors and compelling lines. <br/> <br/>My Opinion: I like the pallette and color balance very much. The muted tones and dreamy quality are wonderfully evocative - it gives the feel that this object is from the fifties because of the blueness of the white. The composition of lines is only slightly off to me - an angle that gives a greater incline to the louvers or a crop or shift to the left would also help, IMO. <br/> <br/>Please let me know if these comments have been of help to you. Feel free to PM me if you have any other questions about my feedback.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Composition: Very intresting. You have strong diagonal lines with excellent forced perspective. I question the crop of the photo - I think I''d like to see the louvers framed to start more to the left for a pleasing line that keeps the eye in frame.  Background: great muted color and soft focus on the grid.  Camera Work: (Focus/DOF/Exposure) Great DOF and focus on the foreground elements. The edges are nice and crisp and add to the color difference along the edge.  Post Processing: n/a The Challenge: Wonderful abstract, great muted colors and compelling lines.  My Opinion: I like the pallette and color balance very much. The muted tones and dreamy quality are wonderfully evocative - it gives the feel that this object is from the fifties because of the blueness of the white. The composition of lines is only slightly off to me - an angle that gives a greater incline to the louvers or a crop or shift to the left would also help, IMO.  Please let me know if these comments have been of help to you. Feel free to PM me if you have any other questions about my feedback.', '2004-05-10 16:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(709256, 73872, 11467, '<td valign="top">Harold, I read it &amp; had a good laugh!<br/>Joe 90, That''s going back a bit, we had that in New Zealand.<br/>Like the picture too by the way!!</td>', 'Harold, I read it & had a good laugh!Joe 90, That''s going back a bit, we had that in New Zealand.Like the picture too by the way!!', '2004-05-10 16:29:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(709372, 73818, 20012, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody for your votes and comments! This is my first challenge entry, and I am quite satisfied with how I did (and with the comments I received ;).<br/> <br/>I agree that the dirt is distracting. The structure of the steps isn''t so bad in my opinion, especially if the image is larger than here.<br/> <br/>Regarding the shadows, I believe that they are important. I also took some pictures where the shadows were not visible, but I like this one better. There is more depth in the image, and it doesn''t become completely abstract. That''s also why I believe that a tighter crop (without the top right corner) would have become too dull.</td>', 'Thanks everybody for your votes and comments! This is my first challenge entry, and I am quite satisfied with how I did (and with the comments I received ;). I agree that the dirt is distracting. The structure of the steps isn''t so bad in my opinion, especially if the image is larger than here. Regarding the shadows, I believe that they are important. I also took some pictures where the shadows were not visible, but I like this one better. There is more depth in the image, and it doesn''t become completely abstract. That''s also why I believe that a tighter crop (without the top right corner) would have become too dull.', '2004-05-10 17:29:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(709451, 72580, 5112, '<td valign="top">Very elegant, love the colours<br/> <br/>edit (addition) The title is great!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-10 16:52:54.</i></td>', 'Very elegant, love the colours edit (addition) The title is great!', '2004-05-10 17:51:47.000000', '2004-05-10 17:52:54.000000', 0),
(709485, 73411, 19780, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully simple. I like the off centered composition. I love the darkness of the red and the sharp focus on the bubbles. At first I thought they were some sort of potato chip ...</td>', 'Wonderfully simple. I like the off centered composition. I love the darkness of the red and the sharp focus on the bubbles. At first I thought they were some sort of potato chip ...', '2004-05-10 18:06:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(709535, 73657, 18709, '<td valign="top">Congrats.   I''m pleased that you have a ribbon.  It is well-deserved.<br/>The detail is highlighted and the work of the sculptor is evident.</td>', 'Congrats.   I''m pleased that you have a ribbon.  It is well-deserved.The detail is highlighted and the work of the sculptor is evident.', '2004-05-10 18:28:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(709537, 73966, 18419, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes and comments.  It turned out to be a very minimalistic picture, but I''m still very happy with it.  Having it off-centered was a conscious decision; I kept thinking about an earlier entry (''Rough and the smooth'' in the Out of place challenge), where many said it was too centered.  I think Melismatica summed it up best here; a bit more ... something would''ve helped put it over the top.<br/>Oh, and no ''1''s!  Woohoo!<br/>Cheers<br/>Stu<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the votes and comments.  It turned out to be a very minimalistic picture, but I''m still very happy with it.  Having it off-centered was a conscious decision; I kept thinking about an earlier entry (''Rough and the smooth'' in the Out of place challenge), where many said it was too centered.  I think Melismatica summed it up best here; a bit more ... something would''ve helped put it over the top.Oh, and no ''1''s!  Woohoo!CheersStu', '2004-05-10 18:29:20.000000', NULL, 0),
