(714477, 73852, 7543, '<td valign="top">*** Greetings from the Critique Club *** <br/> <br/>Hi Wackybill<br/> <br/><b>Challenge</b> <br/>Strictly speaking this shot does not meet the challenge perfectly, you can clearly tell what the subject is and it isn''t that abstract looking. However, it''s not far off and you have a nice shot here. I would think your score has been beaten down due to the fact it doesnt meet the challenge well enough. An extreme closup or an unusual angle would perhaps done better. <br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>What struck me the instant I saw the shot was how the crop was, the lower left part of the branch is partly cut of, a few pixels lower would have been better, or take a different crop and go closer. The lines are nice, branch leading corners together (nice) and the leaf make good elements in the shot. You probably cut the lower end of while shooting and wished you had made another shot with less zoom? (I hate when that happens to me...)<br/> <br/><b>Lighting</b> <br/>Looks like the lighting is natural, It looks nice Background is nicely blurred and dark, leaving the pink flowers up center stage with all the attention. I would like to see the leaf behind the branch a bit brighter though, it does bring a nice element to it and could have been a bit more distinctive from the background.  <br/> <br/><b>Camera work</b> <br/>You''ve got a nice camera there and you seem to know just how to use it, good job. Perfect blurring done, and on f/7.1, perfect balance. No shake or nothing at the focal length, it''s all good. <br/> <br/><b>Post-Processing</b> <br/>The image looks fairly un-edited, and thats always a good thing. Sharp enough (not too much) and the colors are good. Going with no frame was a good idea, since the crop was a bit too tight (not drawing attention to it). Good job here. <br/> <br/><b>Title and Info</b> <br/>Title is very nice. Info is good as well, all aperture etc. info plus the lens used (big plus for my parts). Well done. <br/> <br/><b>Overall (my opinion)</b> <br/>Good shot, technically great but not too interesting for my taste (I''m not a flower fan). Striking contrast on the flowers and background that bring all attention towards the hearts. I gave the shot a 6 during the challenge. <br/> <br/>Hope this helps, <br/> <br/>Best regards, Tyrkinn</td>', '*** Greetings from the Critique Club ***  Hi Wackybill Challenge Strictly speaking this shot does not meet the challenge perfectly, you can clearly tell what the subject is and it isn''t that abstract looking. However, it''s not far off and you have a nice shot here. I would think your score has been beaten down due to the fact it doesnt meet the challenge well enough. An extreme closup or an unusual angle would perhaps done better.  Composition What struck me the instant I saw the shot was how the crop was, the lower left part of the branch is partly cut of, a few pixels lower would have been better, or take a different crop and go closer. The lines are nice, branch leading corners together (nice) and the leaf make good elements in the shot. You probably cut the lower end of while shooting and wished you had made another shot with less zoom? (I hate when that happens to me...) Lighting Looks like the lighting is natural, It looks nice Background is nicely blurred and dark, leaving the pink flowers up center stage with all the attention. I would like to see the leaf behind the branch a bit brighter though, it does bring a nice element to it and could have been a bit more distinctive from the background.   Camera work You''ve got a nice camera there and you seem to know just how to use it, good job. Perfect blurring done, and on f/7.1, perfect balance. No shake or nothing at the focal length, it''s all good.  Post-Processing The image looks fairly un-edited, and thats always a good thing. Sharp enough (not too much) and the colors are good. Going with no frame was a good idea, since the crop was a bit too tight (not drawing attention to it). Good job here.  Title and Info Title is very nice. Info is good as well, all aperture etc. info plus the lens used (big plus for my parts). Well done.  Overall (my opinion) Good shot, technically great but not too interesting for my taste (I''m not a flower fan). Striking contrast on the flowers and background that bring all attention towards the hearts. I gave the shot a 6 during the challenge.  Hope this helps,  Best regards, Tyrkinn', '2004-05-12 15:06:31.000000', NULL, 0),
